.TH SDL_ThreadPriority 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_ThreadPriority \- The SDL thread priority.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_thread.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_ThreadPriority {
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_PRIORITY_LOW,
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_PRIORITY_NORMAL,
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_PRIORITY_HIGH,
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL
.BI "} SDL_ThreadPriority;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDL will make system changes as necessary in order to apply the thread priority\[char46] Code which attempts to control thread state related to priority should be aware that calling
.BR SDL_SetCurrentThreadPriority
may alter such state\[char46]
.BR SDL_HINT_THREAD_PRIORITY_POLICY
can be used to control aspects of this behavior\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

